 "blurb": "The picture is a sheet of glass that shatters from where you set the impact: it breaks into real 3D shards that fly out toward you, fall under gravity, collide and tumble, each shard a piece of glass that refracts the video and catches a bright fresnel glint along its edges, until they clear the frame to uncover what is behind. A native physics bake drives the shards and re-runs the instant you change a setting; a seed makes the break random yet repeatable. Type a range such as (4, 14) into Gravity, Force, Spin, Spread or Piece weight and every shard picks its own value from it; click a shard on the Program monitor to give that one shard its own weight and gravity. Drag the impact on the Program monitor and key Progress, or fire it on the clip's out point.",
